  {
   "text": "The spinner is built in the open design, but it does not pass the plan check yet, so I have not called it finished.\n\n**What's built:** three 25 mm lobes on a 24 mm hub, 8 mm thick, with an 8.4 mm bore. A base disc, an 8 mm axle and a 16 mm retaining cap sit under and over the spinner with 0.4 mm gaps, so it spins free without a bearing. The 0.2 mm radial clearance on the axle is my guess from the clearance guide; a tolerance test will confirm it.\n\n**What fails:**\n- **Overall size:** the lobe tips sit on a 75 mm circle, so the part is 68.3 x 62.5 mm across its bounding box. I wrote 75 x 75 into the plan by mistake. Do you want 75 mm as the circle the tips touch (what it is now), or 75 mm as the bounding box (lobes about 10 percent larger)?\n- **Minimum wall:** the check reads 0.39 mm, which is probably the 0.2 mm bore gap around the axle, not a thin wall. I have not confirmed that.\n- **Feature count:** 3 steps against 6 planned, because the base, axle and cap went in as one step.\n\nNothing has been sliced or sent to a printer. Once you pick the size, I'll fix the outline and re-run the check."
